                <pb facs="0681" n="654" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v23/pg654"/>

                <head>298. Memorandum From Michael V. Forrestal of the National Security Council
                    Staff to Secretary of State Rusk<anchor n="0" xml:id="d298-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-12-18">December 18,
                        1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Emergency Assistance to Indonesia</item>
                </list>
                <p>On December 17, 1962 the President approved the proposal of the Department of
                    State and the Agency for International Development for a $17-million loan to the
                    Republic of Indonesia to finance the emergency importation of certain raw
                    materials and spare parts for Indonesian industry. Procurement is to take place
                    within the United States, and the loan is to be payable in dollars on such terms
                    and conditions as the Department of State and the Agency for International
                    Development deem advisable.</p>
                <p>The President desires that any proposal for additional financial assistance to
                    Indonesia be discussed with him before commitments are made.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">MV Forrestal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
